---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RelatedProducts from '../../components/RelatedProducts.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Costco Hot Dog Menu 2026: Prices, Combos, Sizes & What's New"
  description="Complete Costco hot dog menu: $1.50 combo (dog+bun+soda), water swap option, prices, sizes, nutrition info, and what's new in 2026. Updated July 2026."
  type="article"
  publishedAt="2026-07-17"
  modifiedAt="2026-07-17"
  faqData={[
    { question: "What's on the Costco hot dog menu?", answer: "The Costco food court hot dog menu includes: hot dog ($1.00), hot dog with bun ($1.25), hot dog combo with soda ($1.50), and hot dog combo with water ($1.50). All prices have been unchanged since 1985." },
    { question: "Does Costco still sell the $1.50 hot dog combo?", answer: "Yes. The $1.50 combo (hot dog + bun + 20 oz soda) has been available since 1985 and remains unchanged in 2026." },
    { question: "Can I get water instead of soda with the combo?", answer: "Yes. As of 2026, Costco offers a bottled water option as a replacement for the fountain soda in the $1.50 combo — the first drink change in over 40 years." },
    { question: "Is the hot dog combo available everywhere?", answer: "The $1.50 combo is available at all US Costco warehouses with food courts. International prices vary: CAD $1.50, UK £1.50, Australia AUD $2.00." },
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Costco Hot Dog Menu 2026: Complete Guide to Prices, Combos & Options</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">The Costco food court hot dog menu hasn't changed much in 40 years — and that's exactly why it's legendary. Here's everything on the menu, current prices, and what's new in 2026.</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Quick Answer -->
    <div class="not-prose rounded-xl border border-green-200 bg-green-50 p-6 mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-green-900 mb-4">2026 Hot Dog Menu Prices</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300 text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-green-100">
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Item</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Price</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Includes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 font-medium">Hot dog only</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$1.00</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Frank (no bun)</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 font-medium">Hot dog with bun</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$1.25</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Frank + bun</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-green-50 font-bold"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">🔥 Hot dog combo</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$1.50</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Frank + bun + 20oz soda</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-blue-50 font-bold"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">💧 Combo with water</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$1.50</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">Frank + bun + bottled water (NEW 2026)</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-green-800 mt-3">All prices unchanged since 1985. Available at all US warehouses with food courts.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">The $1.50 Combo: What You Get</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The legendary Costco hot dog combo includes:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-700 mb-4">
        <li><strong>Kirkland Signature all-beef hot dog</strong> (quarter-pound / 4 oz)</li>
        <li><strong>Soft steamed bun</strong></li>
        <li><strong>20 oz fountain soda</strong> with free refills (Coca-Cola, Sprite, Dr. Pepper, etc.)</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Or, as of 2026, you can substitute the soda with a <strong>bottled Kirkland Signature water</strong> at no extra cost — the first drink change to the combo in over 40 years.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">2026 Update: Water Option Added</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">In a historic change to the combo, Costco now offers <strong>bottled water</strong> as a drink option for the $1.50 combo. This is the first modification to the combo drink in over four decades.</p>
      <div class="bg-blue-50 rounded-lg p-5 border border-blue-200 my-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-blue-900 mb-2">What This Means</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-blue-800 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Water replaces the 20 oz fountain soda at no extra charge</li>
          <li>Saves 150-200 calories per combo</li>
          <li>The original soda option with free refills is still available</li>
          <li>Available at participating US warehouses (check with your location)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">This change reflects growing consumer demand for healthier beverage options while maintaining the iconic $1.50 price point.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">International Menu Prices</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">While the US combo stays at $1.50, international prices vary by currency and local costs:</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300 text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-100">
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Country</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">Combo Price</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 text-left">USD Equivalent</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2 font-medium">🇺🇸 United States</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$1.50</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">$1.50</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">🇨🇦 Canada</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">CAD $1.50</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~$1.10</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">🇬🇧 United Kingdom</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">£1.50</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~$1.90</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">🇦🇺 Australia</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">AUD $2.00</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~$1.30</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">🇲🇽 Mexico</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">MXN $30</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~$1.50</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">🇯🇵 Japan</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">¥200</td><td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-2">~$1.35</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Other Food Court Items Often Paired with Hot Dogs</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The Costco food court menu extends beyond hot dogs. Here are the most popular items that shoppers often pair with their hot dog:</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Pizza Slice</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">$1.99 — The other legendary item. Same price since 1977.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Chicken Bake</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">$3.99 — BreadCrunch chicken bake with buffalo sauce.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Soft Serve</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">$1.50 — Dreyer's soft serve, broken only once in history (Jan 1, 2017).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Churros</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">$2.50 — Cinnamon-sugar coated, with chocolate dipping sauce.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="group rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
          <summary class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer">Can I buy a hot dog without a membership?</summary>
          <div class="mt-3 text-gray-700">In most US locations, yes — the food court is accessible without a membership card. Policies vary by location and country.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
          <summary class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer">Does the combo always include a drink?</summary>
          <div class="mt-3 text-gray-700">Yes. The $1.50 price always includes either a fountain soda or bottled water. The soda comes with free refills.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="group rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
          <summary class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 cursor-pointer">Are prices the same at all Costco locations?</summary>
          <div class="mt-3 text-gray-700">In the US, yes. The $1.50 combo price is set at the corporate level and is uniform across all 870+ warehouses worldwide (with local currency adjustments for international locations).</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="my-8">
      <RelatedProducts funnelStage="A" />
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
